 can move away from the city to the suburbs to have a larger living space and be closer to nature.","hypothesis":"To improve his stress and accommodate his living situation with his dogs, Andrew can consider the following potential actions:\n\n1. **Engage in Outdoor Activities**: Andrew finds that nature calms and relaxes his mind. He can take his dogs to trails and dog-friendly spots, which would provide both exercise for the dogs and a stress-relieving environment for himself.\n\n2. **Create a Pup-Friendly Home**: Andrew is planning to make his living space more accommodating for his dogs, which can help reduce stress related to managing their needs in an apartment setting.\n\n3. **Manage Stress through Fun**: Audrey advised Andrew to find ways to manage stress, including having fun. He could incorporate playtime with his dogs or explore new activities that he can do with them.\n\n4. **Consider Doggy Daycare**: Since Andrew mentioned a nearby doggy daycare with a big indoor space, utilizing this service could provide his dogs with socialization and playtime, giving Andrew some relief.\n\n5. **Adopt a Smaller Dog**: Andrew has considered getting another dog, and a smaller dog might be more manageable in an apartment, potentially reducing stress related to space and care.\n\n6. **Incorporate More Plants**: Andrew mentioned getting more plants for his house, which can create a peaceful environment and improve his overall well-being.\n\nBy implementing these strategies, Andrew can work towards reducing his stress while ensuring a comfortable living situation for himself and his dogs.","context":"\nFACTS and ENTITIES represent relevant context to the current conversation.\n\n# These are the most relevant facts for the conversation along with the datetime of the event that the fact refers to.\n# If a fact mentions something happening a week ago, then the datetime will be the date time of last week and not the datetime\n# of when the fact was stated.\n# Timestamps in mem