2-15T00:00:00Z)\n  - Art provides solace for Deborah. (event_time: 2023-04-09T16:30:00Z)\n  - Deborah likes to visit the spot by the water near her mother's old house to reflect and find peace. (event_time: 2023-02-04T09:48:00Z)\n  - Deborah is trying to channel her grief by spending more time with family. (event_time: 2023-01-27T09:49:00Z)\n  - Deborah is channeling her grief. (event_time: 2023-01-27T09:49:00Z)\n  - Deborah implies that these small things connect people to those they have lost and offer comfort. (event_time: 2023-02-04T09:48:00Z)\n  - The dahlias bring peace to Deborah. (event_time: 2023-02-22T16:12:00Z)\n  - Deborah feels peace when sitting in a specific spot by the window at the mother's old house (event_time: 2023-01-27T09:49:00Z)\n  - Deborah does an activity, implied to be coping with grief or viewing photos, at one of the places. (event_time: 2023-01-27T09:49:00Z)\n  - Jolene is glad that Deborah has a location to relax and find peace. (event_time: 2023-08-30T11:46:00Z)\n</FACTS>\n\n# These are the most relevant entities\n# ENTITY_NAME: entity summary\n<ENTITIES>\n  - her memory: Deborah finds peace in keeping her mom's memory alive through art, which brings back powerful emotions and offers comfort after her loss.\n  - Losing someone: Losing someone is hard, but finding coping mechanisms, like art appreciation which connects Deborah to her late mother, is great.\n  - peace: Deborah found hearing stories about her mother emotional but comforting. Deborah later noted that pets bring comfort and peace.\n  - calming: Deborah finds her yoga class calming and likes sharing the exercise because giving people peace and awareness brings her happiness.\n  - family album: Deborah looked at the family album, which contained photos of her parents' 1993 wedding, to find peace after her dad's sudden passing two days prior.\n  - comfort: Deborah found comfort in reconnecting with her mom's old friends, noting how pets also bring comfort and peace.\n  - love